WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.220
 

00:00:01.220 --> 00:00:02.970
In front of me is Grigol
Vashadze.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.549
He is a Georgian politician.

00:00:04.549 --> 00:00:11.360
He used to hold the position of the Minister
of Foreign Affairs under Mikhail Saakashvili

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:18.070
leadership and now he is a presidential candidate,
he is representing the opposition.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.690
Mr. Vashadze, thank you for the interview
and welcome to the program.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:21.890
Thank you very much.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:28.529
- Very interesting fact about you is that
you for a number of years held dual citizenship

00:00:28.529 --> 00:00:33.510
- Russian and Georgian but you renounced the
Russian in 2008.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:41.950
Could you tell more why you decided to give
up your Russian citizenship?

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:50.810
- You know I used to have one passport, just
Russian passport.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:01:06.930
I was residing in Moscow and I had been residing
there from 1976 to 1993.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:13.600
When the Soviet Union collapsed in 1991, I
was in the United States of America.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.000
I don’t remember for five or six months.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.430
And when I came back I discovered that I am
a Russian citizen because Soviet Union didn't

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.430
exist.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:36.480
Then we returned back to Georgia in 2004 and
I got my Georgian citizenship in 2005.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.420
Or four.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.560
Anyway, Four or five.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.780
The end of 2004, the beginning of 2005.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:56.080
And then now after the war, the Russian-Georgian
war I sent my passport to comrade Medvedev

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:02.840
and I said that I am renouncing my Russian
citizenship because I cannot tolerate attitude

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:07.070
of Kremlin towards independence of my country,
of my nation.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:15.160
It took eleven months for Kremlin to decide
if they would like me to sweep me off of my

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:19.250
Russian citizenship but eventually they did.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:25.019
And I am now a holder of just one passport,
of Georgian passport.

00:02:25.019 --> 00:02:31.170
- Mr. Vashadze , there is going to be the
second round of the presidential elections

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:32.170
in Georgia.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:40.489
And as a result of their first round you got
around thirty eight percent of voters’ support.

00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:46.599
And the difference between you and your major
opponent is very insignificant.

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:47.599
Are you happy with the results?

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:59.140
- You know, this is official version of so-called
government and so-called Georgian Dream.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:05.160
In reality I won the first round.

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:13.470
Quite frankly I would not speculate on how
much actually, what percentage actually so-called

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:18.380
Georgian Dream fixed at this election.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:26.060
But the most modest estimate would be 15 percent.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.600
Something like this.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.340
Because Salome Zurabishvili respectfully she
is nobody.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:33.260
Absolutely nobody.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:41.500
It's out of question that thirty eight percent
of Georgians did vote for her.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:50.360
If you just imagine the amount of money spent
by so-called Georgian Dream upon those elections

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:51.360
you are going...

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.360
It's a mind boggling figure.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.129
- So we have unfortunately to rely on the
official data.

00:03:55.129 --> 00:04:04.260
And I would like to ask to analyze these data
because do you think it's a sign, these results,

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:13.819
which were quite unexpected for the ruling
party, these results are a sign of your popularity

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:23.639
among Georgian citizens or it's a sign of
general weariness of the ruling party?

00:04:23.639 --> 00:04:24.870
- Basically all of this.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.850
Combination of all those reasons.

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:36.330
Because when on July the 20th of this year
eight of us, eight of us one of them is sitting

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:44.620
next to me here, eight of us jumped into two
cars and we started our forty three thousand

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.660
kilometer long journey around Georgia.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:52.900
And we said right this time that we're going
to win these elections.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:58.280
Second is that everybody knew me back from
my five years as the Minister for Foreign

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:03.870
Affairs of Georgia and they knew that I've
done a lot of things for this country.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:11.120
That I designed and I brought to the successful
end the campaign of non-recognition of our

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.030
occupied regions.

00:05:13.030 --> 00:05:21.160
Fifty eight states, we have established diplomatic
relations with 58 states we didn't have diplomatic

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.020
relations previously with.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:29.470
I have signed a lot of important treaties
for my country including visa facilitation.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:35.320
Without that agreement with the European Union,
the Schengen zone of the European Union we

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:37.960
could not be having visa liberalization now.

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.070
Then I can go on.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:43.620
So they knew me and my reputation.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:49.110
And the third reason is that Georgian citizen
is outraged.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:57.270
Georgian citizen is very angry Georgian citizen
hates so-called Georgian Dream because Georgian

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:02.780
citizen has not been living so badly since
2004.

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:10.520
And they are not accustomed to live and being
submerged into corruption, crime economic

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:14.740
stagnation, total absence of working places.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:20.080
One hundred fifty thousand kids are living
in hunger, not poverty, but in hunger.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.860
They are going to bed hungry.

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:27.550
Every third citizen is unemployed in this
country.

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:35.199
Close to one million has left this country
since 2012.

00:06:35.199 --> 00:06:40.320
- You are supported by the former president
of Georgia Mikhail Saakashvili.

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:43.580
He's one of your ardent supporters.

00:06:43.580 --> 00:06:48.930
Do you think in the second round it's going
to be an advantage or a disadvantage?

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:54.180
- You know, everybody knows in Georgia that
I am absolutely independent and I was independent

00:06:54.180 --> 00:07:02.740
when I was member of the cabinet from 2008
to 2012.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:06.350
I was not even a member of the party.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:14.490
I absolutely refused to enter and become the
member of this party because I had the extreme

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:20.610
amount of problems with party’s internal
policies.

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.020
And I've been expressing that.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:29.180
As with President Saakashvili I will sum up
my attitude to him.

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:31.360
He is my friend.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:39.370
As each and every sounded lucid Georgian citizen
I'm thankful to him that he has transformed

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:45.380
geographical area into a modern state.

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:49.430
He shall have a right to live in Georgia.

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:53.280
So he shall get back his Georgian citizenship.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:08:02.810
If there are questions which our law-enforcing
agencies or our justice system have to ask

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:05.680
him he shall answer those questions.

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:12.550
And if he is going to have political future
or not, that's up to Georgian nation to decide.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:19.180
- If you become president, you are going to
return his Georgian citizenship?

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:20.180
- Exactly I will.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.350
- Are you going to pardon him?

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.300
- Yes I will.

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:30.560
But I am not going to pardon him I am going
to pardon all political prisoners.

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:37.149
And please don't omit this because some television
channels in Georgia they are cutting the second

00:08:37.149 --> 00:08:39.299
part of this phrase out.

00:08:39.299 --> 00:08:41.000
- I will not cut it.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:42.479
- Of course you will not.

00:08:42.479 --> 00:08:44.879
I will pardon President Saakashvil.

00:08:44.879 --> 00:08:46.769
I will pardon all political prisoners.

00:08:46.769 --> 00:09:00.699
I will pardon all women who did not commit
something beyond imagination and have kids

00:09:00.699 --> 00:09:02.279
outside prison.

00:09:02.279 --> 00:09:06.550
I'm going to do that extremely quickly.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:12.890
Maybe first two or three months because I
know what's going on in prisons

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:20.220
- As a lawyer I want justice to prevail and
justice shall prevail because the third president

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:25.779
of Georgia shall have a right to live here.

00:09:25.779 --> 00:09:29.010
If you're going to use these right or not
it's up to him.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:35.620
Again it's up to him his political future
is up to Georgian people, Georgian citizens.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:45.790
But to reside here in his small house in Guareli
- absolutely we owe to him that much.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:49.769
- You mentioned that you are friends with
Saakashvili.

00:09:49.769 --> 00:09:59.239
But he is absolutely remarkable because he
sometimes resorts to sharp criticism of his

00:09:59.239 --> 00:10:00.939
former allies.

00:10:00.939 --> 00:10:08.470
Do you think that a potential conflict between
you and him if you of course become president

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:14.319
is a workable scenario?

00:10:14.319 --> 00:10:20.870
- You know, it is a strange question because
quite frankly I am not.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:27.420
I have never been choosing my friends according
to their political beliefs.

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:29.290
- You both have political interests.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.290
That's what I meant.

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.290
- Yes.

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:38.970
He's my friend and if there is a contradiction
between my beliefs and his beliefs I'll try

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:42.569
my best to retain our friendship.

00:10:42.569 --> 00:10:50.149
But quite possibly our political paths will
part away.

00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:51.509
I would not.

00:10:51.509 --> 00:11:03.449
I would not start screaming like some of his
other friends to TV correspondents that Misha

00:11:03.449 --> 00:11:08.009
Saakashvili is the only one to be blamed for
the mistakes.

00:11:08.009 --> 00:11:15.259
That Misha Saakashvili is a dictator, Misha
Saakashvili was an obstacle when those guys

00:11:15.259 --> 00:11:17.940
were doing all the job to transform Georgia.

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.619
To me it's ridiculous.

00:11:19.619 --> 00:11:22.790
- He is not a dictator, he is a true democrat?

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.949
- He absolutely.

00:11:24.949 --> 00:11:30.009
Which dictator ever staged peaceful transition
of power.

00:11:30.009 --> 00:11:36.079
- Mr. Vashadze, you're absolutely right with
your great example of Mr. Saakashvili being

00:11:36.079 --> 00:11:39.779
a true democrat that he ensured peaceful transition
of power.

00:11:39.779 --> 00:11:47.920
It's out of question and I think it's one
of the fundamental things for Georgia to preserve

00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:50.019
this democratic tradition.

00:11:50.019 --> 00:12:01.389
But his critics say that when in power he
was extremely violent with his political opponents

00:12:01.389 --> 00:12:09.519
that he put them in prison that there were
numerous violations of human rights.

00:12:09.519 --> 00:12:13.410
There was a demonstration a peaceful demonstration
2007.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:22.839
And he used some methods to disseminate this
demonstration.

00:12:22.839 --> 00:12:26.749
What could you answer to this criticism?

00:12:26.749 --> 00:12:34.430
- When we're speaking about mistakes we shall
differ mistakes from dictatorship.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:37.509
Because if you would like to remember 2007.

00:12:37.509 --> 00:12:48.399
Yes, it was a very sad occasion in our history
but again nobody was dispersing this crowd

00:12:48.399 --> 00:12:51.790
incredibly large crowd in front of the parliament.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:57.239
And they had constitutional right for assembly.

00:12:57.239 --> 00:13:02.269
They had constitutional right to express their
opinion and for free speech.

00:13:02.269 --> 00:13:04.079
I can tell you from my standpoint.

00:13:04.079 --> 00:13:14.619
This raid that was exercised against and inside
TV IMEDI that was incredible mistake, political

00:13:14.619 --> 00:13:15.619
mistake.

00:13:15.619 --> 00:13:18.459
Incredible political mistake.

00:13:18.459 --> 00:13:25.980
And I think that in many ways it was the beginning
of the end.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:34.230
And my answer about Misha I could tell you
with 100 percent certainty that he is too

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.949
young to be written off.

00:13:35.949 --> 00:13:43.449
But as each and every person who actually
did spend five or six years in immigration

00:13:43.449 --> 00:13:48.880
he will have to accustom to this country from
the scratch, because this country has changed

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:50.490
and it has changed significantly.

00:13:50.490 --> 00:13:54.809
- What do you mean under change?

00:13:54.809 --> 00:13:58.809
Is Georgia still a democracy?

00:13:58.809 --> 00:14:00.709
- It is

00:14:00.709 --> 00:14:05.319
- It has become more democratic since Mr.
Saakashvili left

00:14:05.319 --> 00:14:14.709
- No less democratic, it became less democratic
because if you check those facts of election

00:14:14.709 --> 00:14:23.470
fixing, if you go through our TV market and
discover that there is only basically one

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:28.449
important independent TV station Rustavi-2.

00:14:28.449 --> 00:14:38.129
If you go through Internet information hubs
and you discover that basically nearly 99

00:14:38.129 --> 00:14:41.179
percent of them are controlled by so-called
Georgian Dream.

00:14:41.179 --> 00:14:44.129
By Ivanishvili through all this.

00:14:44.129 --> 00:14:49.980
Of course it's less democratic but the major
freedoms are here.

00:14:49.980 --> 00:14:51.899
We have...

00:14:51.899 --> 00:14:56.670
And Ivanishvili with his so-called Georgian
Dream is chicken pox.

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:58.730
Do you know what chicken pox?

00:14:58.730 --> 00:14:59.730
Ветрянка.

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:06.449
Ветрянка, которой в детстве
болеют и вот переболеешь

00:15:06.449 --> 00:15:13.360
and after three first days you're having temperatures
over 40 or 41.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:17.459
Then after three days you are quickly recovering.

00:15:17.459 --> 00:15:21.359
So we are having Ivanishvili as a chicken
pox.

00:15:21.359 --> 00:15:24.480
- Mr. Vashzdze, returning to the presidential
election.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:31.910
According to the current Georgian constitution
the role of the president is quite symbolic.

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:35.879
So it has effectively no executive powers.

00:15:35.879 --> 00:15:43.059
Why are these elections important for you
personally and for the country?

00:15:43.059 --> 00:15:48.970
- Yes, you would like to ask me why these
elections were so heated.

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:55.100
It's very correct and timely answer because
it's no not only presidential elections but,

00:15:55.100 --> 00:16:02.109
it also most importantly, it's a referendum
on the future of our country.

00:16:02.109 --> 00:16:04.309
Everybody understands that.

00:16:04.309 --> 00:16:09.810
When we are winning not even when we are winning
those elections we are winning the referendum

00:16:09.810 --> 00:16:15.779
on our country and we are bringing closer
snap parliamentary elections.

00:16:15.779 --> 00:16:17.569
Everybody understands that, too.

00:16:17.569 --> 00:16:23.079
Second it's utter nonsense that President
of Georgia is not going to have enough powers.

00:16:23.079 --> 00:16:29.259
Excuse me, Supreme Commander of armed forces
much as far as I know it's a good point.

00:16:29.259 --> 00:16:31.009
- But as far as I know.

00:16:31.009 --> 00:16:34.079
It is a good point but you cannot execute
this even function without the consent of

00:16:34.079 --> 00:16:35.790
the parliament or the government?

00:16:35.790 --> 00:16:41.869
- Yes, it is Cardinal Richelieu, who used
to say: “Patience”.

00:16:41.869 --> 00:16:42.869
- Ok

00:16:42.869 --> 00:16:50.350
- Supreme Commander, the chief representative
of country in international relations.

00:16:50.350 --> 00:17:02.699
Power of veto, power to approve Prime Minister,
power of pardon and a lot of other but most

00:17:02.699 --> 00:17:03.699
important.

00:17:03.699 --> 00:17:05.020
And don't forget, please.

00:17:05.020 --> 00:17:09.530
There is a spirit of Constitution and there
is a letter of constitution.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:18.679
Spirit of constitution means political process
and nobody can curb me to be head of the political

00:17:18.679 --> 00:17:19.679
process.

00:17:19.679 --> 00:17:26.370
I can see any government not only of so-called
Georgian Dream but any government, when I

00:17:26.370 --> 00:17:34.070
ask 50 or 100 thousand my citizens to go out
in the street and join my protest for something.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:38.139
Who is going to curb that right?

00:17:38.139 --> 00:17:40.789
Just imagine yourself.

00:17:40.789 --> 00:17:44.190
What kind of demonstration we're going to
stage.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:50.200
So so-called Georgian Dream is very –very
right when they're fighting a deadly fight

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:53.690
for this post but they lost that fight.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:58.659
- You mentioned a very interesting fact that
you think that these are not just presidential

00:17:58.659 --> 00:17:59.659
elections.

00:17:59.659 --> 00:18:03.019
This is a referendum about the future of the
country.

00:18:03.019 --> 00:18:11.850
Now in the second round you and your opponent
Mrs. Zurabishvili are left.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:17.940
If we do not focus on who supports whom you
are supported by Mikhail Saakashvili and his

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:24.919
political party whereas Zurabishvili is supported
by Ivanishvili and Georgian Dream.

00:18:24.919 --> 00:18:30.799
What are their ideological differences between
you and your opponent?

00:18:30.799 --> 00:18:36.840
I think that you agree on the western power
of the European path for Georgia on NATO accession

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:37.840
on everything.

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:43.049
- I am supported by I am supported trust me
by well over 40 percent of Georgian citizens.

00:18:43.049 --> 00:18:45.380
This is the most important thing for me.

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:50.389
When it comes to differences I will tell you
what the differences are.

00:18:50.389 --> 00:18:56.679
So-called Georgian Dream and their candidate
campaniero Zurabishvili, they think that everything

00:18:56.679 --> 00:18:59.090
is wonderful in Georgia.

00:18:59.090 --> 00:19:00.850
They think that the economic situation.

00:19:00.850 --> 00:19:06.059
She has just said that the economic situation
is not that bad as you're describing it.

00:19:06.059 --> 00:19:10.539
Not to me, to the audience and to journalists.

00:19:10.539 --> 00:19:12.779
Ivanishvili thinks that everything was perfect.

00:19:12.779 --> 00:19:18.440
I mean for five years he gave a paradise to
Georgian citizen.

00:19:18.440 --> 00:19:23.919
Then suddenly he jumped out and said that
I have just discovered that one million are

00:19:23.919 --> 00:19:25.009
living in poverty.

00:19:25.009 --> 00:19:31.000
Whenever they got those outrageous reports
from the World Bank the United Nations and

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.540
UNICEF.

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:40.720
They are scared to death because they understand
Georgian citizens are deprived of all achievements

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:48.080
economic achievements which the government
gave to them from 2004 to 2012.

00:19:48.080 --> 00:19:51.759
Country is submerging into extreme poverty.

00:19:51.759 --> 00:19:53.200
This is the difference.

00:19:53.200 --> 00:20:00.070
We are screaming that we shall abolish in
our budget all the luxuries.

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:06.509
Those stupid expenses which are made just
to win elections.

00:20:06.509 --> 00:20:15.409
Financing all these all these soccer programs
and I don't know baseball team and Georgian

00:20:15.409 --> 00:20:17.789
ice hockey team.

00:20:17.789 --> 00:20:22.710
Can you imagine the idiocy of these?

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:29.179
When Ukrainian and Bulgarian hockey players
are playing in the fourth or fifth league.

00:20:29.179 --> 00:20:32.419
I don't remember where.

00:20:32.419 --> 00:20:41.210
We shall canalize all these money to health
care, to social assistance, to education and

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.409
to defense.

00:20:42.409 --> 00:20:45.080
Otherwise we're going to disappear as a nation.

00:20:45.080 --> 00:20:48.620
Our demography is catastrophic.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.809
That's what we differ on.

00:20:50.809 --> 00:20:56.460
And those excuse me my Georgian and those
idiots are proposing to this country marijuana

00:20:56.460 --> 00:21:00.379
plantations is as a local motion for our economy.

00:21:00.379 --> 00:21:07.320
In the 21st century is an epoch of economy
of knowledge.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:12.441
When we shall jump on the train which is going
to the 22nd century otherwise we are going

00:21:12.441 --> 00:21:16.289
to become for forever losers.

00:21:16.289 --> 00:21:17.289
And I don't know.

00:21:17.289 --> 00:21:18.289
Marginal state you know limiter of state.

00:21:18.289 --> 00:21:23.879
They are calling our civil society our non-governmental
organizations fascists.

00:21:23.879 --> 00:21:27.019
Those idiots do not even know meaning of this
word.

00:21:27.019 --> 00:21:28.740
Do you know who is doing this?

00:21:28.740 --> 00:21:30.009
- Ivanishvili, I know.

00:21:30.009 --> 00:21:35.960
But he said that it was not a correct word
to use.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:38.539
- What was correct?

00:21:38.539 --> 00:21:39.539
Nazi?

00:21:39.539 --> 00:21:40.539
- No-no-no.

00:21:40.539 --> 00:21:42.740
He acknowledged that it wasn't.

00:21:42.740 --> 00:21:44.170
It was the wrong thing to do.

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:45.170
That's what I wanted to say.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:46.330
- But he said what he's thinking.

00:21:46.330 --> 00:21:49.409
I don't care about his excuses and his partners.

00:21:49.409 --> 00:21:55.240
I do not because they said that they're going
to bang opposition on the head.

00:21:55.240 --> 00:22:00.929
The speaker of Parliament they have this Clockwork
Orange you know as a speaker of parliament

00:22:00.929 --> 00:22:04.280
who said that he is going to bang opposition
on the head.

00:22:04.280 --> 00:22:07.460
I'm very happy that he got banged on the head
after the first tour.

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:08.499
So that's where we differ.

00:22:08.499 --> 00:22:10.039
- You have another major difference.

00:22:10.039 --> 00:22:18.129
I don't want to talk about your differences
with Ivanishvili but we are talking about

00:22:18.129 --> 00:22:21.350
you and your opponent.

00:22:21.350 --> 00:22:22.700
And of course you have absolutely different
backgrounds.

00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:28.649
You have a lot in common because Mr. Zurabishvili
used to hold the position of the Minister

00:22:28.649 --> 00:22:31.929
of Foreign Affairs und also Saakashvili leadership.

00:22:31.929 --> 00:22:34.129
She was before you.

00:22:34.129 --> 00:22:40.220
She is a French career diplomat she was born
in France and you are a Soviet career diplomat.

00:22:40.220 --> 00:22:42.370
Do you have problems with this?

00:22:42.370 --> 00:22:43.370
- No.

00:22:43.370 --> 00:22:56.150
I do not have any problems with it because
a person who was born in 1958 in Tbilisi you

00:22:56.150 --> 00:22:59.289
couldn't be anything else.

00:22:59.289 --> 00:23:07.070
So I was a Soviet diplomat and I can tell
you I am very proud of it.

00:23:07.070 --> 00:23:15.559
Because I participated in negotiations which
made our life safer: prohibition of Chemical

00:23:15.559 --> 00:23:21.110
Weapons and prohibition of nuclear tests.

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:29.790
And I went through a fantastic school.

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:35.929
I don't know what professional qualifications
of Zurabishvili are.

00:23:35.929 --> 00:23:36.929
Excuse me.

00:23:36.929 --> 00:23:45.960
But I shall repeat these words but when people
are saying in the street that I am the best

00:23:45.960 --> 00:23:53.149
Minister for Foreign Affairs in our history
I'm very proud of it.

00:23:53.149 --> 00:23:57.789
So-called Georgian Dream and Ivanishvili’s
TV stations they tried to play on this that

00:23:57.789 --> 00:24:03.309
I am a KGB agent, I am Russia’s influence
agent.

00:24:03.309 --> 00:24:06.630
I am this, I am that.

00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:09.390
It Didn't work at all .

00:24:09.390 --> 00:24:12.160
- If you win their elections.

00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:16.419
What reaction on the part of the Russian government
do you expect?

00:24:16.419 --> 00:24:22.830
- I spent five years of my life fighting with
Russia and I succeeded and left Russia in

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:27.919
a shameful company of Venezuela Syria Nicaragua
and no.

00:24:27.919 --> 00:24:33.730
- So you're still going to meet with Putin
to discuss the future of the occupied territories?

00:24:33.730 --> 00:24:35.570
То есть вы не планируете
встречаться с Путиным для

00:24:35.570 --> 00:24:36.570
обсуждения будущего оккупированных
территорий?

00:24:36.570 --> 00:24:37.570
- No.

00:24:37.570 --> 00:24:43.820
No because I don't know what the reaction
of Kremlin is going to be.

00:24:43.820 --> 00:24:48.720
I mean we are speaking about your country.

00:24:48.720 --> 00:24:50.220
You're Russian.

00:24:50.220 --> 00:24:59.850
Georgia by its independence took the strategic
role away from Russia itself in Caucuses.

00:24:59.850 --> 00:25:03.080
And Russia is fighting to return that back.

00:25:03.080 --> 00:25:10.730
But trouble is that two occupied regions,
they are not solving Russian problem at all.

00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:15.640
They are suitcases without a handle you know
you can’t throw them away because it's a

00:25:15.640 --> 00:25:16.640
shame.

00:25:16.640 --> 00:25:19.400
You cannot keep them because you do not need
it.

00:25:19.400 --> 00:25:21.929
You are just wasting your money upon it.

00:25:21.929 --> 00:25:22.940
This is what's happening.

00:25:22.940 --> 00:25:27.530
I don't know what the Kremlin's reaction is
going to be and quite frankly I don't care.

00:25:27.530 --> 00:25:28.530
!!!!

00:25:28.530 --> 00:25:32.480
- Who is your role model among present or
past world leaders?

00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:33.720
- George.

00:25:33.720 --> 00:25:34.960
Marshall.

00:25:34.960 --> 00:25:36.659
- And why?

00:25:36.659 --> 00:25:40.149
- This is the man who won the Second World
War.

00:25:40.149 --> 00:25:45.779
Don't believe that Soviet Union could win
this war without the United States military

00:25:45.779 --> 00:25:47.140
and logistical assistance.

00:25:47.140 --> 00:25:48.140
You are.

00:25:48.140 --> 00:25:53.200
You are young and they will be telling to
you that we could win this war alone.

00:25:53.200 --> 00:25:54.460
Forget about it.

00:25:54.460 --> 00:25:57.989
- Mr. Vashadze, I would like to thank you
for the interview and for your time.

00:25:57.989 --> 00:25:58.989
- Thank you.

00:25:58.989 --> 00:25:59.889
It was pleasure to be with you.

